            <ArticleTitle>Sonography in the diagnosis of acute appendicitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>465-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute appendicitis can be a diagnostic dilemma. The classic triad of leukocytosis, pain at McBurney's point and a history compatible with appendicitis has a diagnostic accuracy rate of only 80 percent. Ultrasonography, combined with this triad, can improve the diagnostic accuracy, decreasing the negative laparotomy rate from 20 percent to less than 10 percent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
